# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Read by `loadDeployEnv()` in
# src/deploy-notify.js, which is called by bin/production-deploy.js before it
# reports the deploy — and only these two names are read, so this file cannot
# be used to inject anything else into a deploy.
#
# The file has to exist on whichever machine runs the deploy. In practice that
# is the server: `ssh ovh 'cd /opt/tailchat && node bin/production-deploy.js'`
# inherits nothing from a shell profile, and the checkout is the one place both
# a laptop and the server always have. Keep it 0600; it is a bot token.
#
# TOKEN: from @BotFather, the `123456789:AA…` string.
# CHAT: where the report goes — a personal chat id (a positive number, what
# the bot sees as `message.chat.id`) or a channel/group id (negative,
# `-100…`). The bot must have been started by that chat, or be an admin of
# that channel, or Telegram answers 403.
TAILCHAT_DEPLOY_TG_TOKEN=
TAILCHAT_DEPLOY_TG_CHAT=
